# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #method-parts, #fields; Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-24 Q1 (a)): the first for argument int(i, 0)
# is an explicit declaration of i, so under call: S D it writes the i place of D, as every declaration of an inline
# body does. The loop runs over D: D\total becomes 0 + 1 + 2 = 3, D\i ends at 3, the pad of D keeps 1. Entry 7.
S:
    int: total 0
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 3) i++
        total: total + i
    end: for
end: S
D:
    int: i 9
    int: pad 1
    int: total 5
end: D
call: S D
int: r 81
if: D\total = 3 && D\i = 3 && D\pad = 1
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
